[Desktop Entry]
Version=1.0
Name=X
Exec=omarchy-launch-webapp https://x.com/
Terminal=false
Type=Application
Icon=x
StartupNotify=true
StartupWMClass=org.gnome.Epiphany.WebApp_x_com

# X, as a web app (docs/apps.md B1-B3).
#
# Upstream ships this entry, byte for byte, in /usr/share/omarchy/applications.
# Nothing on this phone copies it into a place the drawer reads -- only
# omarchy-refresh-applications does that, and this project never runs
# upstream's installer -- so it is repeated here, with the one key upstream has
# no reason to carry.
#
# StartupWMClass is that key. omarchy-launch-webapp runs a web app as its own
# Epiphany profile named org.gnome.Epiphany.WebApp_<host with dots underscored>
# (bin/omarchy-launch-webapp says why it must be named that), and that is the
# app id its window arrives with. The shell indexes entries by their startup
# class, so without this line the recents card and the shade's notification
# card for X would have no entry to take a name or an icon from, and the card
# would read org.gnome.Epiphany.WebApp_x_com.
#
# It names Epiphany's class because Epiphany is this phone's browser
# (docs/apps.md). Installing a Chromium-family browser changes the class, and
# the line then matches nothing -- which is what it did before it was here.
